## Phase 3: Reporting to Bug Bounty Triage Teams
When submitting this finding to a program platform (like [YesWeHack](https://www.yeswehack.com/)), follow these critical formatting tips to get your submission accepted: [7] 

* Do not use alert(1) in production: Triagers often close reports with raw alert(1) popups as spam. Always leverage alert(document.domain) to definitively prove your payload has completely broken past the origin server sandboxes. [5] 
* Provide clear impact scope: Explain that an attacker can chain this flaw to execute arbitrary commands, rewrite page DOM nodes dynamically to steal credentials, or hijack active user session cookies. [2, 5] 

